From 90e50a15c6c0f42de08598cc178c180220820d98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 19:42:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/28] base: provide pre-MMU virtual memory on AROS

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-phase-3

AI_STATUS: complete

ROOT_CAUSE: AROS has no sys/mman API, while native V8 requires aligned reservations, partial release, permission transitions, decommit, discard, and file mappings.

FIX_REASON: Back reservations with page-aligned Exec allocations, track contiguous live ranges for trim/free, emulate commit state by zeroing, keep protection transitions explicit no-ops, and load/write mapped files through serialized seek I/O.

SCOPE: src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-headless -j4 obj/v8/libv8_libbase.a

RISK: high; this is a functional single-process pre-MMU model, not isolation, true lazy commit, or cross-process shared mapping, and must be replaced by OPAL/MMU backing.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc | 256 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 252 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

